  ],
  "oracle_attribution": "IP64_DNS64_DROP is the PR's purpose, not an incidental fixture helper. It is the return value ip64_dns64_4to6() yields for a message it cannot translate and the signal ip64_4to6() checks (if (len == IP64_DNS64_DROP) return 0;) to drop a half-rewritten reply instead of forwarding it, which is the defect the PR closes. The macro is absent at base (base ip64-dns64.h has no such #define) and the fixed test asserts len == IP64_DNS64_DROP, so the native test binary is source-blocked at base; the missing interface is the very interface the tests need.",
